{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1396803-dorohedoro","id":1396803,"title":"Dorohedoro","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-15T21:20:23-07:00","id":1396803,"title":"Dorohedoro","content":"This is an interesting anime Netflix show I happened upon on a whim and it really reminds me of Mage! I only have watched the first episode so far, but basically from what I gathered so far is that the setting is in a dystopian world-scape that comprises two areas: The Hole- a decrepit city where all the &quot;Sleepers&quot; (the regular people are basically Sleepers since they don't have magic) reside and another realm where all the Sorcerers (Awakened in this sense of the anime). The Sorcerers use The Hole as a testing ground for their spells/rotes. From what I've seen so far in the anime is that this Awakened-esque faction that has control of the setting are Life sphere focused, since their main paradigm entails transmorgifying people into animal-like people or general change things.<br /> <br /> This is where our protagonist comes in, a man turned Lizardman who wants above all else wants to kill all Sorcerers and return back from his &quot;curse&quot; that was bestowed upon him by some random Sorcerer/Mage. The specific foci that the Sorcerers use to achieve their magic/effects seems to be in the form of pointing out their fingers (the two main characters, the Lizardman and his restaurant owner sidekick routinely exploit this), in which some strange black mist emanates from them to either kill or transform a target. These &quot;Awakened&quot; in Dorohedoro also seem to be adept in Correspondance since they can invoke doors move back and forth to their realm of residence from The Hole (I don't know if they can use this technique to go anywhere else, I only just finished ep. 1).<br /> <br /> It basically feels like some sort of chronicle or alternate universe where somewhere along the line some new Disparate faction somehow won the Ascension war and now they have shaped the Consensus where all their effects are considered coincident because they'v successful shifted the public conscious Paradigm or just got collectively strong enough to brute force it. Sorry, I just had to nerd out when I had seen an anime that just seemed so close to something that could be from WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}